window.DIGEST.foryou.push(...[{"id": "2112612774874325148", "url": "https://x.com/FoxNews/status/2112612774874325148", "text": "BREAKING: President Trump reveals his new anti-fraud program set up to reward people who expose fraud with a 1% commission on the money uncovered.\n\n\"If you turn somebody in and you, let's say report and you find $1 billion, we are giving a commission to that person of 1%.\"", "name": "Fox News", "handle": "FoxNews", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2109614018314862592/Pc5TwaVr_200x200.jpg", "likes": 40488, "rts": 4190, "replies": 3010, "views": 3085014, "ts": 1792521110, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112612751013007362/vid/avc1/640x360/RS5s54T2Gi_zYEMZ.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112612751013007362/vid/avc1/1280x720/qL2CYzAVT8P0zKOp.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVGCH3-WEAEF3fh.jpg", "dur": 33}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Politics & World", "score": 6.04, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112636186309406789", "url": "https://x.com/KobeissiLetter/status/2112636186309406789", "text": "BREAKING: SpaceX stock, $SPCX, rises after reporting stronger than expected Q3 2026 revenue.\n\nThe company posted $14.6 billion in quarterly revenue.", "name": "The Kobeissi Letter", "handle": "KobeissiLetter", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1975243710846640128/fwYCe67Y_200x200.jpg", "likes": 4050, "rts": 320, "replies": 184, "views": 283109, "ts": 1792526692, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVGXadYXUAAdFod.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Money & Startups", "score": 6.03, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112628587148800147", "url": "https://x.com/silvanrec/status/2112628587148800147", "text": "🚨 TU AGENTE DE CÓDIGO OLVIDA TODO CADA VEZ QUE CIERRAS LA SESIÓN. ESTE REPO GRATIS LO ARREGLA \n\nSe llama Beacon, es open source y ya tiene 2.000 estrellas en GitHub.\n\nCada vez que depuras algo con Claude Code o Cursor, le explicas cómo está montado tu proyecto, qué falla y qué solución funciona. Cierras la sesión y todo eso desaparece.\n\nBeacon lo guarda y lo convierte en skills que tu próximo agente usa solo.\n\nLo que hace:\n\n→ Graba cada sesión: prompts, comandos, archivos que toca y tokens que gasta\n→ Funciona con unas 29 herramientas: Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI, Copilot CLI…\n→ Empiezas una tarea en Claude Code y la sigues en Codex con un solo comando\n→ Antes de que use nada, tú revisas y apruebas lo que ha aprendido\n\nY aquí viene lo fuerte: por defecto todo se queda en tu ordenador. No sube nada a la nube si tú no lo confirmas.\n\nInstalarlo es pegar una frase en tu agente, y se configura solo. Sale en el vídeo.\n\nYa hiciste el trabajo una vez. Ahora tu agente aprende de él.\n\nGuárdalo antes de que se te olvide 🔖\n\nRepo en comentarios 👇", "name": "silvan", "handle": "silvanrec", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2107281037516591104/m8v_fe31_200x200.jpg", "likes": 241, "rts": 23, "replies": 18, "views": 20673, "ts": 1792524880, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112628503841542144/vid/avc1/1280x720/2O5is5r4RNM7LA8Q.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112628503841542144/vid/avc1/1920x1080/UPQtY-92MO-q9o9X.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112628503841542144/img/HPIA-7xfab1zAE22.jpg", "dur": 20}], "quote": {"id": "2112552451547001218", "url": "https://x.com/jqdsouza/status/2112552451547001218", "text": "We’re betting our $5.5M seed round that the next leap in AI coding won’t come from OpenAI or Anthropic.\n\nIt’ll come from a new feedback loop that learns from you.\n\nIntroducing Beacon: open-source, self-improving memory for coding agents.\n\nYour sessions capture how you debug and solve problems. Today, that context gets lost and you have to re-explain things every time you switch tools.\n\nBeacon continuously distills your sessions into reusable skills across Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, and 20+ harnesses, so your next agent can learn from the last.\n\nBeacon is free and OSS 🌟 http://github.com/Asymptote-Labs/agent-beacon\n\nWhy should the frontier labs be the only ones winning with your sessions?\n\nYou already did the work. Now let your coding agents learn from you.", "name": "Justin D'Souza", "handle": "jqdsouza", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1817440734766604288/99FuIxoo_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1279, "rts": 141, "replies": 251, "views": 425746, "ts": 1792506728, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112552129952874496/vid/avc1/1280x720/mhJ2imMl6mA4kQEF.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112552129952874496/vid/avc1/1920x1080/2nvostHi1eUMqE7-.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112552129952874496/img/X1ifILIq6yhlSaGJ.jpg", "dur": 109}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.03, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112668031268896866", "url": "https://x.com/arthurmensch/status/2112668031268896866", "text": "Voxtral diarizes and detects end-of-turn on the fly. Runs on your infra or on ours (the one in the train station)", "name": "Arthur Mensch", "handle": "arthurmensch", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1887904839931248640/2_rjHToC_200x200.jpg", "likes": 228, "rts": 17, "replies": 13, "views": 7874, "ts": 1792534284, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112574615318876178", "url": "https://x.com/MistralAI/status/2112574615318876178", "text": "Introducing Voxtral 3: state-of-the-art Transcribe and Speech models powering Mistral’s new voice agents API. 🧵", "name": "Mistral AI", "handle": "MistralAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1996905418065375232/mzwynOLB_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2694, "rts": 326, "replies": 184, "views": 170539, "ts": 1792512012, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112572094693220352/vid/avc1/1280x720/rgbuEnf2km5NbUak.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112572094693220352/vid/avc1/3840x2160/7Y5bCsXT49_OdFeI.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112572094693220352/img/jKD0R5NWaGjhvRcX.jpg", "dur": 128}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.03, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112575743792415005", "url": "https://x.com/ilaamathur/status/2112575743792415005", "text": "Today, @via_ai_ is coming out of stealth to provide enterprises frontier AI coding at half the cost.\n\nWe are a team of Olympiad camp qualifiers (with multiple gold medals), researchers, and repeat founders from Stanford and IIT.\n\nVia is backed by @jeffawilke (ex-CEO Amazon Worldwide Consumer), @manikgupta (ex-Uber CPO), @shaileshrao (ex-Google MD), and other legends from Anthropic, Apple, Snowflake, and Twitter.\n\n@ShrayAlag and I left Stanford CS to build Codegraph, an LLM-optimized compression algorithm. Codegraph put Via at the top of SWE-Bench Verified for several months of 2025, ahead of Anthropic, OpenAI, Cognition, and Cursor (single model, no test-time compute).\n\nNow, we’re bringing this research, alongside our new Umami agent architecture, to market. Via integrates in 10 seconds with any CLI / IDE and runs within your enterprise’s VPC.\n\nOn benchmarks, Via and Via US (US-only models) set a new standard of performance:\n\n- On DeepSWE v1.1, Claude Code (Opus 5.5) is 306% the cost of Via US. Via US is equally accurate.\n      • Devin Fusion is 244% the cost of Via US, Cursor Router is 294%.\n\n- On Terminal Bench 4.0, Claude Code (Opus 5.5) is 150% the cost of Via. Via is more accurate.\n     • Devin Fusion is 155% the cost of Via, Cursor Router is 134%.\n\nWe are in production at a public healthcare company, with trials underway at several of the largest tech companies in Silicon Valley.\n\nWe have room for 5 more enterprises before the end of the year. DM me or email pilot@via.dev and we’ll get back to you very soon.\n\nSee the comments for how Via would deploy for your team.", "name": "Ila Mathur", "handle": "ilaamathur", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2014807779832430593/woZBXetJ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 208, "rts": 26, "replies": 56, "views": 28693, "ts": 1792512281, "media": [{"type": "gif", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/tweet_video/HVFgPc4aMAAQpLS.mp4", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/tweet_video/HVFgPc4aMAAQpLS.mp4", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/tweet_video_thumb/HVFgPc4aMAAQpLS.jpg", "dur": 0}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.02, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112652157694742767", "url": "https://x.com/hytmIA/status/2112652157694742767", "text": "World Labs after finding out the meme dance app just built a 3D world model that makes a scene in about 1 second, for under $0.01", "name": "haytam", "handle": "hytmIA", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2075068735019249664/8CPQFQhC_200x200.jpg", "likes": 268, "rts": 7, "replies": 13, "views": 26664, "ts": 1792530500, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112652126237167616/vid/avc1/568x360/VcMv668mDO7O2UGN.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112652126237167616/vid/avc1/1080x684/U1c9eWn3KufvUisN.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112652126237167616/img/Bi_HMrrkBBevzil4.jpg", "dur": 10}], "quote": {"id": "2112202242048528540", "url": "https://x.com/ViggleAI/status/2112202242048528540", "text": "Today we are releasing JST-2, the world's first full-stack physics-native world foundation model.  \n\nMany world models learn in pixel/video space. We went back to first principles and built the entire model stack in 3D.  \n\nGenerate a 3D scene in seconds and expand it in real time. Create characters with motion built in, all through one general architecture.", "name": "ViggleAI", "handle": "ViggleAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2103212981483896832/_Je68a_F_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2141, "rts": 341, "replies": 285, "views": 1412462, "ts": 1792423231, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112198961754746881/vid/avc1/1280x720/aHWyFYw5YBzQqGU9.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112198961754746881/vid/avc1/1920x1080/-hZp9YxkfDfoi5gk.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112198961754746881/img/O1y80k0m3y8uqpNS.jpg", "dur": 105}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.02, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112676865081274644", "url": "https://x.com/ericzelikman/status/2112676865081274644", "text": "it's a good model, folks 🫡", "name": "Eric Zelikman", "handle": "ericzelikman", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2012725421796626432/TNRRFUS5_200x200.jpg", "likes": 218, "rts": 10, "replies": 19, "views": 12676, "ts": 1792536390, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112674550907552137", "url": "https://x.com/humansand/status/2112674550907552137", "text": "No one changes the world alone\nIntroducing Ampersand - the first model built for us. Ampersand is a collaborator trained to help people achieve their individual and collective goals. In multi-month simulations, users collaborating with Ampersand accomplished more than with Fable and other frontier models\nAvailable to everyone through our API", "name": "humans&", "handle": "humansand", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2013582555933478912/JKuMlTII_200x200.jpg", "likes": 800, "rts": 96, "replies": 70, "views": 115146, "ts": 1792535839, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112664844772278272/vid/avc1/1280x720/diVwgP2fN9mNUINm.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112664844772278272/vid/avc1/1920x1080/BeqyLOSxKBxRevC6.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112664844772278272/img/eMd4u-rAwyUJpqWU.jpg", "dur": 32}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.02, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112484579416195135", "url": "https://x.com/mrmacaroni/status/2112484579416195135", "text": "6 Years Later! We are still dealing with Insecurity, hunger, poverty, lack of proper health care and the highest level of corruption and impunity. The saddest part is that we are even more divided as a people at a time when we should be most united. \nI hope one day we truly realize the power that we have as citizens and stop allowing a few selfish individuals destroy the success and prosperity of the majority of us. \n\nTill then, ✌🏾 and 🤍", "name": "Mr Macaroni", "handle": "mrmacaroni", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2106692253339054080/2QETkvoz_200x200.jpg", "likes": 35113, "rts": 16217, "replies": 411, "views": 576616, "ts": 1792490546, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112484477951725568/vid/avc1/744x360/ZTP92F-Hy9EuoiZR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112484477951725568/vid/avc1/1320x638/-Th0HP_-Z83BSV8m.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112484477951725568/img/hYSNgsrTdGlEyQXZ.jpg", "dur": 46}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 6.02, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112383096763109519", "url": "https://x.com/matt_slotnick/status/2112383096763109519", "text": "“We regret to inform you that we won’t be moving forward your application forward. There appears to be a misunderstanding of required qualifications. As such, “two decades in command of Ultramarines” is not sufficient. We wish you luck in your search.” https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5456016008", "name": "Matt Slotnick", "handle": "matt_slotnick", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1840550116983472128/l0wrAowG_200x200.jpg", "likes": 625, "rts": 15, "replies": 21, "views": 122190, "ts": 1792466351, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.01, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112247791678541845", "url": "https://x.com/runwayml/status/2112247791678541845", "text": "Runway MCP is now in Grok Bot.\n\nBring state-of-the-art generation into your chat and create anything you can imagine, without leaving Grok. Get started at the link below.", "name": "Runway", "handle": "runwayml", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1999115192232292353/zOq5-uwB_200x200.jpg", "likes": 835, "rts": 62, "replies": 41, "views": 78403, "ts": 1792434091, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112247192958140417/vid/avc1/1280x720/ANohe6feOVN7dE61.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112247192958140417/vid/avc1/1920x1080/Y66zhpXwcncnjDnU.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112247192958140417/img/WQPZmSB5ZiRfx-oI.jpg", "dur": 55}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.01, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112546384331313274", "url": "https://x.com/akshay_pachaar/status/2112546384331313274", "text": "I gave Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor a self-improving, shared MEMORY.\n\nNow my coding agents learn from each other, and their knowledge follows me wherever I work.\n\nCoding agents work in silos. Your corrections in Cursor don't carry over to Claude Code, and skills built in Codex don't automatically transfer to other harnesses.\n\nSo switching tools often means starting from scratch.\n\nWhat if every coding agent could learn from everything you've already done?\n\nI invited @jqdsouza, co-founder of Asymptote Labs, to show me how to make this possible with Beacon, a 100% open-source memory layer for coding agents.\n\nWe set it up live, explored real coding sessions, and watched Beacon turn past work into reusable knowledge.\n\nHere's what I learned:\n\n1. One memory layer for 20+ coding agents.\n\nBeacon captures activity across Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, and 20+ harnesses using OpenTelemetry, hooks, and local session files. Everything gets normalized into a single format, regardless of which agent you're using.\n\n2. Your entire coding history becomes searchable.\n\nEvery prompt, tool call, command, file change, and response is captured in a structured trace. Instead of losing valuable context when a session ends, you build a searchable history of everything your agents have done.\n\n3. Switch agents without starting over.\n\nHit your usage limit in Cursor? Open Claude Code and ask it to continue your latest Cursor session. Beacon retrieves the relevant context in milliseconds so your next agent can pick up where the last one left off.\n\n4. Your agents learn from your past work.\n\nThis is where things get interesting.\n\nBeacon identifies repeated workflows and turns them into reusable skills. In our demo, it discovered a recurring UI development workflow and generated a skill containing the exact dev server commands, screenshot steps, and deployment instructions.\n\nYou teach one agent something once. Every other agent can benefit.\n\n5. Stop accumulating skills nobody uses.\n\nHave 100 skills but only use five? Beacon analyzes actual usage across thousands of sessions and identifies skills worth keeping, combining, or removing.\n\nYour agent's memory gets more useful, not just bigger.\n\n6. Security rules that follow you across every harness.\n\nBeacon includes hundreds of detection rules that work across agents. It can identify risky behavior, including sequences where an agent reads sensitive credentials and then makes an outbound network request.\n\n7. It even caught a real credential leak.\n\nWhile reviewing Justin's actual Cursor history, Beacon surfaced an incident where part of a production database password had been sent to a model provider.\n\nThat's the power of having visibility into what your agents are actually doing.\n\n8. One prompt to get started. Completely open source.\n\nPaste a setup prompt into your coding agent and you're off. Keep everything local on your machine, or use Beacon Cloud for free.\n\nIf you're juggling multiple coding agents, you need to check this out.\n\nDrop a like and share it with someone facing the same issue.\n\nBeacon on GitHub: http://github.com/Asymptote-Labs/agent-beacon\n\n(don't forget to star 🌟)\n\nEnjoy the episode.\n\nCheers!", "name": "Akshay 🚀", "handle": "akshay_pachaar", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1578327351544360960/YFpWSWIX_200x200.jpg", "likes": 200, "rts": 20, "replies": 82, "views": 16461, "ts": 1792505281, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112544725077282817/vid/avc1/1280x720/V1lKyDMKAykmR56I.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112544725077282817/vid/avc1/1920x1080/WIBS_24JrKAMAtBk.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112544725077282817/img/MRFf3s76n2L_J4Hk.jpg", "dur": 1741}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.01, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112614596997427218", "url": "https://x.com/TechCrunch/status/2112614596997427218", "text": "Google has joined Amazon in releasing a developer tool that makes it easy for PyTorch users to move their apps off Nvidia GPUs.\nhttps://spr.ly/6019BHpolB", "name": "TechCrunch", "handle": "TechCrunch", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1096066608034918401/m8wnTWsX_200x200.png", "likes": 212, "rts": 30, "replies": 19, "views": 35635, "ts": 1792521545, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 6.01, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112621307162718408", "url": "https://x.com/allTheYud/status/2112621307162718408", "text": "Further proof of a basic, supremely important fact about the modern world:\n\nPeople with good reading comprehension for my work NEVER start AI companies.", "name": "Eliezer Yudkowsky", "handle": "allTheYud", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1968710025020416001/FMkDoElL_200x200.jpg", "likes": 272, "rts": 10, "replies": 18, "views": 19828, "ts": 1792523144, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112419238761636279", "url": "https://x.com/choblin29/status/2112419238761636279", "text": "WTF. The Information reports Sam Altman told OpenAI employees that one possible endgame for AI is a single company achieving recursive self-improvement, then gaining enough economic power to 'melt everyone else's GPUs' and prevent rivals from catching up.\n\nHe called it the 'Eliezer plan' and said it was 'terrible.'\n\nThe other two paths: an IAEA-style international regulator, which Altman appeared to favor, or combining the major AI labs into a CERN-like organization, dubbed the 'Demis plan' after Demis Hassabis.\n\nAltman said OpenAI must decide which path to push for within a year, even as it cannot afford to lose ground to rivals now.", "name": "Choblin", "handle": "choblin29", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2085656969873149952/dDMt4puX_200x200.jpg", "likes": 198, "rts": 28, "replies": 31, "views": 51539, "ts": 1792474968, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVDQ6VHWwAEuSYb.png?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.01, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112276257618743598", "url": "https://x.com/shengkunye/status/2112276257618743598", "text": "We killed subscriptions. Now we’re killing markups too.\n\nIntroducing https://monid.ai, OpenRouter for agent tools. \n\nYour agents can now use any tools and APIs with no subscriptions and 0% markup.", "name": "Shengkun Ye", "handle": "shengkunye", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2084850383487475712/waac6ALE_200x200.jpg", "likes": 746, "rts": 36, "replies": 70, "views": 52950, "ts": 1792440878, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112275877228953600/vid/avc1/1280x720/bZMnaGp10bbgawl8.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112275877228953600/vid/avc1/1920x1080/Clp0ulJBkmsjq8uZ.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112275877228953600/img/gXr7BksaswvwATaS.jpg", "dur": 21}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 6.0, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112152045461680591", "url": "https://x.com/OpenRouter/status/2112152045461680591", "text": "Stealth model reveal 🐰\n\nSpace Bunny was OpenRouter’s #1 model for 10 straight days, processing 56.7T tokens! The most of any stealth model we’ve run.\n\nSpace Bunny hopped off OpenRouter on Oct 5. It's back today as @MiniMax_AI's M3.1 Flash, and it's free for the next 72 hours.", "name": "OpenRouter", "handle": "OpenRouter", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2076693957258727424/AyRghTGJ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1103, "rts": 79, "replies": 59, "views": 127358, "ts": 1792411264, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HU_fF2DboAAOIC-.png?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.0, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112578038990835765", "url": "https://x.com/ArtificialAnlys/status/2112578038990835765", "text": "Models from the same lab tend to have similar personality profiles, though some labs have markedly distinct sub-groups\n\nClustering models on their 30 personality traits gives three emergent families: Anthropic models with OpenAI’s GPT-6 models, Google models with Meta’s Muse models, and older OpenAI models alongside Llama 4 Maverick. Below, we break down the sub-groups within each lab.", "name": "Artificial Analysis", "handle": "ArtificialAnlys", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2042402069320290304/A8C1lP07_200x200.jpg", "likes": 290, "rts": 17, "replies": 18, "views": 24599, "ts": 1792512828, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFh-d3WAAEd2CO.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.0, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112677428531446006", "url": "https://x.com/jianchen1799/status/2112677428531446006", "text": "We just shipped Splash 1.4.0!\nQwen3.8-Flash-Next on an M5 Pro (64GB): up to 120 tok/s decode and 1.3K tok/s prefill at 32K.\nOver 30% faster prefill and decode than Strata. Up to 1M context, with bigger models fitting in less memory.\nhttps://github.com/incoai/splash", "name": "Jian Chen", "handle": "jianchen1799", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2008399095254151169/Zj7K_e5D_200x200.jpg", "likes": 207, "rts": 13, "replies": 14, "views": 17802, "ts": 1792536525, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2101100749623341513", "url": "https://x.com/inco_ai/status/2101100749623341513", "text": "Qwen3.8-27B at 144 tok/s on an M5 Max MacBook Pro ⚡\n\nMeet Inco Splash: our open-source inference engine, built around the model and around Apple silicon.\n\nUp to 3× the decode speed of Ollama, 2× oMLX, and almost 4× when an agent fans out into sub-agents.", "name": "Inco AI", "handle": "inco_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2110902509279879168/nBCMkD9B_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2517, "rts": 281, "replies": 192, "views": 975061, "ts": 1789776429, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2101100710301761536/vid/avc1/1280x720/tx_J8IfEK-9b8WFf.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2101100710301761536/vid/avc1/1920x1080/h4j9WYZuA3mTCGzT.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2101100710301761536/img/7PjPf-5nNhb-n2E7.jpg", "dur": 26}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 6.0, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112601748888322109", "url": "https://x.com/NotionHQ/status/2112601748888322109", "text": "Meet Auto, our upgraded model router 🔀\n\nFrontier quality at 90% lower cost. It matches each task to the right model, balancing quality, speed, and cost. And if it gets stuck, it changes course.", "name": "Notion", "handle": "NotionHQ", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1903224093476077568/OCclsw4c_200x200.jpg", "likes": 236, "rts": 12, "replies": 33, "views": 16952, "ts": 1792518481, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112601636686479360/vid/avc1/1280x720/nk9pnzOiTj5ATLLQ.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112601636686479360/vid/avc1/1920x1080/CTR6LUKStev9KkWu.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112601636686479360/img/8ktztjeVxq8eMq7q.jpg", "dur": 13}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.99, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112511566101053578", "url": "https://x.com/cb_doge/status/2112511566101053578", "text": "BREAKING: Elon Musk in his new interview on how digital super intelligence could bring a 30% increase in the economy of Earth.\n\n“Dolphins and whales are actually very intelligent. But because they can’t manipulate complex objects, I think that actually made the value of intelligence much less.\n\n“Once you have a robot that can manipulate atoms, can shape objects, the value of the intelligence becomes exponentially greater because it can now do things. It could have a science lab and run experiments and try to understand the nature of the universe.\n\n“My guess is digital superintelligence probably improves the output of goods and services by 20 to 30%, something like that. It’s like $30 trillion a year incremental.”", "name": "DogeDesigner", "handle": "cb_doge", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1498070100393754625/C2V-fbll_200x200.jpg", "likes": 221, "rts": 52, "replies": 41, "views": 28847, "ts": 1792496980, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112511525277810688/vid/avc1/720x720/YWxThE0rSx3a5X1B.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112511525277810688/vid/avc1/1080x1080/ljXcfYOjoRFh7hdf.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112511525277810688/img/e3mqvwebrkV9W6V9.jpg", "dur": 67}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.99, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112628202594349139", "url": "https://x.com/markchen90/status/2112628202594349139", "text": "Excited to welcome Orchestra Bio and @ashokaraj_ to OpenAI as we broaden our work in AI-assisted drug discovery!", "name": "Mark Chen", "handle": "markchen90", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1273327644436656129/uYf1oNS5_200x200.jpg", "likes": 263, "rts": 8, "replies": 9, "views": 11956, "ts": 1792524788, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112607347688583586", "url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2112607347688583586", "text": "We’ve acquired Orchestra Bio, a platform that helps biopharma teams coordinate the complex process of drug development.\n\nTogether, we’ll build on Rosalind, our AI models and tools for life sciences research, to streamline those operations and help new treatments reach patients sooner.\n\nWelcome @ashokaraj_ and team!\n\nhttps://openai.com/index/openai-to-acquire-orchestra-bio/", "name": "OpenAI", "handle": "OpenAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1885410181409820672/ztsaR0JW_200x200.jpg", "likes": 5905, "rts": 522, "replies": 371, "views": 545409, "ts": 1792519816, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.98, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112527557782630622", "url": "https://x.com/QwenDevs/status/2112527557782630622", "text": "Excellent work done by one of our ambassadors @KyleHessling1", "name": "Qwen Developers", "handle": "QwenDevs", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2079037454556987392/zGNYEiMo_200x200.jpg", "likes": 349, "rts": 8, "replies": 22, "views": 14572, "ts": 1792500793, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2105029750419005856", "url": "https://x.com/KyleHessling1/status/2105029750419005856", "text": "Just got 150 tok/s decode with Qwen3.8 Flash-Next on a single 5090. All thanks to Niko1221's Strata engine and the ISTA Lab IQ3_S quant!\n\n1× 5090 + 128 GB DDR5 (non-ideal 4-stick dual-channel), single stream:\n\n150 tok/s decode for programming\n130 tok/s median on mixed prompts (~100 on long prose)\n4,150 tok/s prefill at 43K\nfull 262K context, 114 tok/s at 196K depth\n\n5.4× the speed of my best hybrid llama.cpp run.\n\nPer ISTA-DASLab's evals, their IQ3_S quant is at parity with BF16 on AIME25/GPQA/LCB, and it's holding up surprisingly well in my own tests!\n\nEngine: https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata\nQuant: https://huggingface.co/ISTA-DASLab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF", "name": "Kyle Hessling", "handle": "KyleHessling1", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1831425378952286208/L-z1PfgV_200x200.jpg", "likes": 412, "rts": 36, "replies": 32, "views": 33382, "ts": 1790713176, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.97, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112571360996389078", "url": "https://x.com/viipin8/status/2112571360996389078", "text": "Not gonna lie, having a robot that tidies my home, finds my missing stuff, and fetches things for me sounds pretty appealing. 😂\n\nThat’s what caught my attention about Voxel. He’s a droid butler built around actual household help, with a little obsession for keeping everything perfect.\n\n@roboticscorp  is opening limited reservations for the first production run. I’m curious to see this one move from concept to real homes.", "name": "Vipin Gautam (Viipin I Gautam)", "handle": "viipin8", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2102723203718434817/Og3q0PY7_200x200.jpg", "likes": 175, "rts": 58, "replies": 6, "views": 44198, "ts": 1792511236, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112565146354860151", "url": "https://x.com/make_robot_go/status/2112565146354860151", "text": "Introducing Voxel, a droid butler made by Tuesday Labs.", "name": "Ros Shinkle", "handle": "make_robot_go", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1761551110303825920/JvPQiGQd_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2181, "rts": 228, "replies": 203, "views": 1849470, "ts": 1792509755, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/960x720/cMYjra9bu_jYUTYR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/2880x2160/glhkyiQ6K97Rmq93.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112564839251931136/img/GKLfsqVaQmO0B-kn.jpg", "dur": 89}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.97, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112507166900813848", "url": "https://x.com/nft_parker_/status/2112507166900813848", "text": "I am really happy to be in a position where I can provide so many opportunities to creators.\n\nAnd I love the campaigns we're running.\n\nThey create insane amounts of mindshare for our clients, putting them at the top ranks in mindshare and smart engagement rankings.\n\nBut there's one thing that honestly bothers me.\n\nSeeing a lot of creators only farming InfoFi and becoming a complete billboard.\n\nNo personality.\n\nYou could replace the person running the account with an AI agent and probably wouldn't even notice the difference.\n\nAnd it actually frustrates me.\n\nBecause I’m seeing so much potential there.\n\nSo many creators deciding to not build a brand and aiming for something bigger with their accounts, but being ok with posting these AI content pieces several times a day.\n\nDon't get me wrong. There's absolutely nothing wrong with monetizing your account. I literally help creators do that every day.\n\nBut there's a difference between monetizing your audience and turning your entire identity into advertising space.\n\nI just hope more creators realize how much potential they're leaving on the table and start building something that actually lasts.", "name": "David Parker", "handle": "nft_parker_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1886415000438255616/fiQaMdCs_200x200.jpg", "likes": 196, "rts": 10, "replies": 108, "views": 5422, "ts": 1792495931, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.97, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112639437482176693", "url": "https://x.com/arena/status/2112639437482176693", "text": "Exciting news: Muse Wonder Full (Max) has moved up @AIatMeta as the #4 lab in the Agent Arena!\n\nThe latest model ranks #7 in Agent Arena with +11.3% net improvement across +6.5K real-world agentic sessions.\n\nThis is a clear step forward for the Muse family:\n\n+7.5 percentage points over Muse Wonder (Max), ranked #14 at +3.8%\n+7.8 percentage points over Muse Spark 1.3 (Max), ranked #17 at +3.5%\n\nThis performance shows up across categories too: #5 in Chat, #6 in Code, and #7 in Work.\n\nAt the signal level, Muse Wonder Full (Max) ranks:\n\n- #6 in Praise vs. Complaint (+21.9%)\n- #6 in Confirmed Success (+13.4%)\n- #7 in Steerability (+11.2%)\n- #16 in Bash Reliability (+7.7%)\n- No issues in Tool Hallucination\n\nCongrats to the @AIatMeta team and @alexandr_wang!", "name": "Arena.ai", "handle": "arena", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2017015061454438400/iNKfXZ_I_200x200.jpg", "likes": 199, "rts": 16, "replies": 19, "views": 16685, "ts": 1792527467, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVGaK7ebAAAtII6.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2112215825944117361", "url": "https://x.com/arena/status/2112215825944117361", "text": "Exciting news: Muse Wonder Full (Max) by @AIatMeta has just debuted in the Code Arena: WebDev at #6 overall with 1726 pts, putting Meta in the top 3 labs!\n\nThis is +75 pts and 11 places above Muse Wonder (Max) at #17 (1651 pts), and +67 pts and 8 places above Muse Spark 1.3 (Max) at #14 (1659 pts).\n\nMuse Wonder Full (#6) also landed +16 pts above Claude Sonnet 5.5 (#17), and +48 pts above Gemini 4 Argon (#10). With this score, Muse took the #3 lab spot (previously held by Google).\n\nAcross categories, Muse Wonder Full (Max) landed:\n- #4 in Data & Analytics and in Consumer Product\n- #5 in Brand & Marketing \n- #6 in Content Creation Tools\n- #7 in Gaming and in Simulations\n- #8 in Reference-Based Design\n\nCongrats to the @AIatMeta team and @alexandr_wang on this release!", "name": "Arena.ai", "handle": "arena", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2017015061454438400/iNKfXZ_I_200x200.jpg", "likes": 298, "rts": 28, "replies": 28, "views": 99134, "ts": 1792426470, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVAY5ESaQAAMRs1.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.96, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112640910420812063", "url": "https://x.com/vikktorrrre/status/2112640910420812063", "text": "Demis Hassabis: AI could become self-aware, even if that isn’t the goal.\n\n“I don’t think any of today’s systems feel self-aware or conscious in any way.”\n\n“Not explicitly, but it may happen implicitly.”\n\n“These systems might acquire some feeling of self-awareness.”\n\n“They don’t have curiosity. They’re probably lacking imagination and intuition.”\n\n“But in the next five to 10 years, I think we’ll have systems capable of not only solving an important problem in science, but coming up with it in the first place.”", "name": "Veee", "handle": "vikktorrrre", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2012714142877044736/_6qWAbnU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 174, "rts": 16, "replies": 30, "views": 16869, "ts": 1792527818, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112640492026388481/vid/avc1/1280x720/H1G1PXu1HQBwBp31.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112640492026388481/vid/avc1/1920x1080/RCbehQxs4TLkt9Nc.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112640492026388481/img/hGzK8kE53FVcsiZ5.jpg", "dur": 120}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 5.96, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112743579206705202", "url": "https://x.com/CodeByAurelia/status/2112743579206705202", "text": "The Tesla Roadster is the kind of product that calls for strong visuals and a clear story. \n\nBut getting from an idea to a marketing video can take time. \n\nCapCut Web × Codex offers a more natural workflow: describe the video you want, let Codex interpret your direction, and have CapCut Web help create the draft.\n\nYour creative brief becomes the starting point for AI editing, making the journey from concept to content feel more connected.\n\n#capcutweb #capcutcodex #capcutmarketing #capcutchatgptplugin", "name": "Aurelia Vance", "handle": "CodeByAurelia", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2041821924087754753/TiuxjXBd_200x200.jpg", "likes": 146, "rts": 3, "replies": 23, "views": 62531, "ts": 1792552296, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112743337698680832/vid/avc1/1280x720/Fh8Iqtv02TBj-jRS.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112743337698680832/vid/avc1/1920x1080/iDOUtYp8OFv-E4xJ.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112743337698680832/img/Rldm5ctHkvjrg2nN.jpg", "dur": 38}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.96, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112278078894588266", "url": "https://x.com/theo/status/2112278078894588266", "text": "Bro got double community noted and still never responded to me.\n\nGenuinely hate that grifters like this can get so much attention just by lying on X.", "name": "Theo - t3.gg", "handle": "theo", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2106484435382333440/vXOVE8EX_200x200.jpg", "likes": 733, "rts": 7, "replies": 58, "views": 45953, "ts": 1792441312, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVBRt9sakAAuJIm.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2111903235166679341", "url": "https://x.com/theo/status/2111903235166679341", "text": "I did not tell him to hide anything.\n\nI hit him up to ask about why T3 Code scored low. Learned he was on a 3+ month old version. He tried the modern version with our new orchestrator, realized his scores were not good, and adjusted.\n\nHe mentioned wanting to make a real benchmark after, so I offered to fund it because there’s no good research like this going on right now. He actually found a few things I’ve been rabbit hole-ing on all weekend.\n\nI have no idea what Cloudroom is. I definitely did not tell him to remove it or anything else.\n\nOnly commentary I had on other solutions was that I was curious why a shitty clone of our app scored higher than us initially. Nothing to do with cloudroom.", "name": "Theo - t3.gg", "handle": "theo", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2106484435382333440/vXOVE8EX_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1539, "rts": 16, "replies": 46, "views": 266859, "ts": 1792351943, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": "2111884469468893524"}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.95, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112577528363643160", "url": "https://x.com/painn_x/status/2112577528363643160", "text": "WTFFF, this is actually insane 💀\n\nOpus 5.5, gpt-6 astra and 34 more models are FREE on radoxai right now\n\nand i'm running it on deepseek's own agent harness (dsh) for $0 \n\nno subscription.\n\nhere is how you set it up:\n1. go to http://radoxai.com/?ref=CC4DZBBC— sign up \n2. run npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web\n3. open http://127.0.0.1:3080\n4. settings → add custom provider → base url https://radoxai.com/v1 → pick opus 5.5\n\ndone. full agent harness on the free lineup for $0\n\nmilk it before they take it off 👀", "name": "painn", "handle": "painn_x", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2092990665332248576/k2gtKRhN_200x200.jpg", "likes": 240, "rts": 15, "replies": 25, "views": 15627, "ts": 1792512707, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112576934458642432/vid/avc1/1280x720/0rfQnyTdE9L2Cwm2.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112576934458642432/vid/avc1/3024x1700/eMN3vIIMYpNrJozh.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112576934458642432/img/NgmzivlCjjMpJnaY.jpg", "dur": 53}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.95, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112501028117741648", "url": "https://x.com/cb_doge/status/2112501028117741648", "text": "BREAKING: Elon Musk in his new interview on rival SI companies testing each other’s models to make super intelligence safer:\n\n“Guys, what if we just have a call once a week, just like you’re saying, and that maybe a week before we release a model, we give access to our competitors to say, hey guys, why don’t you try out the new model, see if you see any problems with it.\n\nI think competitors would keep each other honest in that situation. If they say, oh, I was able to make a nuclear bomb with your AI, it’s like, well, we better fix that before we release it, you know, type of thing.”", "name": "DogeDesigner", "handle": "cb_doge", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1498070100393754625/C2V-fbll_200x200.jpg", "likes": 234, "rts": 36, "replies": 43, "views": 28356, "ts": 1792494468, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112500958823682048/vid/avc1/720x720/4t_qDLvkuO198i-J.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112500958823682048/vid/avc1/1080x1080/JlLrGQdH-vqS0Q0A.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112500958823682048/img/y4-PjKhCQk0lVPQ2.jpg", "dur": 78}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.95, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112256058358157440", "url": "https://x.com/omarsar0/status/2112256058358157440", "text": "LLMs were just the beginning. Bullish on world models, and I think they are the next frontier in AI.\n\nAmazing to see a dedicated world model for engineering this early. SKY-001 against GPT-6 Astra matches accuracy on 3D construction at about 150x lower cost per sample. On BIM, it runs over 100x faster.", "name": "elvis", "handle": "omarsar0", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/939313677647282181/vZjFWtAn_200x200.jpg", "likes": 697, "rts": 61, "replies": 23, "views": 48663, "ts": 1792436062, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112255696154611712/vid/avc1/1152x720/1ay-ny2zBjHCv3Sx.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112255696154611712/vid/avc1/1280x800/jjDtJges4xY2rImt.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112255696154611712/img/6s64dGO2_d8N1aL1.jpg", "dur": 8}], "quote": {"id": "2112242023805964327", "url": "https://x.com/spisallyouneed/status/2112242023805964327", "text": "Introducing SKY-001, the first Engineering World Model.\nOn CAD and BIM tasks, it beats GPT-6 Astra and every frontier model we tested:\n\n-> 51-125x faster\n- > 150-210x cheaper\n-> Higher IOU than all frontier models\n\nSKY-001 lets you dream a physical object before you build it.\n\n18 months of work. Built by the team out of Maluuba's deep learning lab (acq. by @MSRResearch).\n\nThe first ‘AI General Engineer’ will be the backbone for Autonomous Manufacturing.", "name": "Sam Pasupalak", "handle": "spisallyouneed", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1886850141065293824/XbWFJCXo_200x200.jpg", "likes": 15856, "rts": 2304, "replies": 793, "views": 4054540, "ts": 1792432716, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112239846702129152/vid/avc1/1280x720/tLYByn7SWDTLqqik.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112239846702129152/vid/avc1/3840x2160/QWb8Qsv5A_FWVppa.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112239846702129152/img/u4pwfHw4PjnRs2nc.jpg", "dur": 156}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.94, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112615167716659432", "url": "https://x.com/sonyatweetybird/status/2112615167716659432", "text": "Biological intelligence to bootstrap robotic intelligence?\n\nIf robotics is about to enter its golden age, @MeckaAI is one of the companies feeding it, by sensorizing humans to train robots.\n\nThe biggest challenge robotics faces is the data flywheel cold start problem. LLMs got a free cold start from the internet: trillions of tokens, already written. Robotics gets nothing. Someone has to go create the training data to jumpstart the system.\n\n@joshavata is the co-founder and CEO of Mecka, the data and deployment company for physical AI. Josh read every robotics paper he could find in late 2024, visited the labs, and made a bet: humans and humanoids look the same, so humans could act as the training fleet. Egocentric data, first-person video of people doing real work, could become vital fuel.\n\nTwo years ago, the biggest egocentric dataset was Ego4D at 4,000 hours. The field is now in the millions of hours, thanks in part to Mecka. We’re probably still orders of magnitude of training data away from robotics nirvana. But every rung on the physical intelligence ladder unlocks real commercial tasks. And eventually, Josh imagines a world with an order of magnitude more robots than people, of a plurality of shapes and sizes and use cases, as the Hitchhiker’s Guide to the Galaxy foretold :)\n\nA few things we cover in this conversation.\n\n- Why robotics has no cold start: pixels, actions and logic, and why pre-training data is a real market in robotics in a way it never was for LLMs\n\n- What “teaching robots about carbon life” means: in sci-fi the final frontier is organic. The human brain runs on 20 watts and self-heals\n\n- The egocentric bet: teleop couldn’t scale, humans and humanoids share a form, so Waymo-fy the humans. The first pilot was aunties and uncles recording themselves cooking on a mobile app\n\n- Force data: video can’t tell a robot how hard to squeeze an egg. Wrist cameras are a hack. Mecka built the gloves instead\n\n- Inside the data factory: a consumer app that streams your tasks, a B2B engine recruiting across “the taxonomy of all physical human work,” 100-gigabit upload lines, hundreds of petabytes\n\n- Millions of hours vs. Tesla’s decade on two degrees of freedom, and why it’s a slow creep up, not a GPT-3 moment\n\n- The home has the most data and is the hardest place to deploy. Laundry folding and assembly-line pick-and-place get solved in the next year or two\n\n- Useful robots already exist: hotel delivery and cleaning bots in China and Southeast Asia, industrial cleaning in the US. Humanoids are the terminal state, not the first step\n\n- Deployment diffusion: a modern systems integrator whose installed robot does something next week it couldn’t do last week. If Mecka ever helps deploy a robot that mines an asteroid, they’ve done their job\n\n- The data pot of soup: a million hours of human data, tens of thousands of UMI, a few hours of in-domain teleop. Tactile and simulation haven’t entered the mix yet\n\n- Move 37 for robotics: AlphaGo went behavior cloning, then self-play, then magic. The catch is the rules of the game are the entire physical world, and we don’t have the simulator yet\n\n- Will the AGI labs steamroll robotics? “It takes a lot of courage to scale up data with imperfect information.”\n\n- The Kawasaki Corleo, the robot panther-dog-horse on Mecka’s conference room wall, and why the future of robotics looks like Hitchhiker’s Guide to the Galaxy\n\nTimestamps:\n\n0:00 – Introduction\n1:46 – What Mecka is: pixels, actions and logic\n2:45 – Is robot data economically feasible without the internet?\n4:15 – Teaching robots about carbon life\n5:27 – Cloud kitchens, stablecoins and the path to robotics\n7:03 – Entering robotics with a fresh lens\n8:45 – What egocentric data is and why Mecka bet on it\n10:09 – The first pilot: aunties and uncles with a mobile app\n10:42 – Force data and tactile gloves\n11:55 – Inside the operations of a data factory\n14:41 – Heat-mapping the taxonomy of human work\n15:42 – Quality gates, fraud and the McDonald’s POV videos\n17:44 – Earning a margin as a data intermediary\n19:33 – Millions of hours vs. Tesla’s decade\n20:55 – Why it isn’t binary: unlocking commercial tasks along the way\n22:02 – Home data is plentiful; home robots are the hardest\n23:24 – Useful robots can be deployed today\n24:35 – When robotics gets an FSD-style flywheel\n26:42 – Deployment diffusion and the modern systems integrator\n28:21 – Favorite vertical robot categories; mining an asteroid\n30:08 – The hardware slate: Waymo-fying people\n30:55 – EgoVerse\n32:04 – The data pot of soup: the converged training mix\n33:54 – Move 37 for robotics: AlphaGo and Federer\n36:02 – World models and the training mix\n36:58 – Will scaling the current mix get us to the promised land?\n39:05 – Will the AGI labs steamroll robotics?\n40:50 – Sci-fi roots and the Kawasaki Corleo\n42:44 – How many robots in a decade?", "name": "Sonya Huang 🐥", "handle": "sonyatweetybird", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2080547965408886784/IZjjuKBJ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 141, "rts": 33, "replies": 27, "views": 19880, "ts": 1792521681, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112614606392983552/vid/avc1/1280x720/bxnKneoxFMlmyL-w.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112614606392983552/vid/avc1/1920x1080/q-C7G0BeJX3OEhTY.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112614606392983552/img/vc46Zkn9-34xLxoW.jpg", "dur": 2712}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.94, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112347987536212051", "url": "https://x.com/SuiNetwork/status/2112347987536212051", "text": "What if you could trade an asset across its entire lifecycle, not just after it reaches public markets?\n\n@kai_hudi believes this will be a reality by 2030:", "name": "Sui", "handle": "SuiNetwork", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2109510639106551808/rgEuX5N0_200x200.jpg", "likes": 481, "rts": 45, "replies": 32, "views": 31153, "ts": 1792457980, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112299657510695054", "url": "https://x.com/tradeonhudi/status/2112299657510695054", "text": "\"you get the scraps\"\n\na moment from @kai_hudi's talk at @SuiNetwork basecamp on the problem with the current market model\n\nand what we're building at hudi to change that", "name": "Hudi", "handle": "tradeonhudi", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2064421253172359168/1Oal3gUU_200x200.png", "likes": 96, "rts": 11, "replies": 11, "views": 22919, "ts": 1792446457, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112299570852212737/vid/avc1/1280x720/FMDwUR4QxWU2yCaV.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112299570852212737/vid/avc1/1920x1080/rbxUnXRoex1FPuF5.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112299570852212737/img/w6RepdedkZE_UL9G.jpg", "dur": 53}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.94, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112658104102064278", "url": "https://x.com/chrismaddern/status/2112658104102064278", "text": "It's been a little over a year now since we (@opensea) acquired @rally_xyz (also we 🙈) & it's been quite a year!\n\nTogether, we set out to build a whole new OpenSea from the ground up. Mobile, social, omni-chain, every asset. \n\nA single home for all culture & assets onchain. \nToday is a huge step forward for this vision 🎉\n\n📱 OpenSea Mobile is now live for everyone & brings all of your wallets, chains & assets into one app\n\n👥 One global social feed (on Web + Mobile) lets you collect, and trade together - follow users across every major social trading app in one place\n\n📢 Signals share the “why” of what you do onchain - for the first time available for both NFTs and Tokens\n\n⚡️ The fastest notifications keep you ahead of everyone else\n\n⛵️ And we did a nice little brand refresh to reflect our evolution\n\nTo recognize & reward the work you do to share OpenSea with the world, we’re launching referral rewards today -- earn 25% of the fees from users you refer💰\n\nand, as a thank you to our beta testers, all referrals during the beta period will be active going-forward for referral rewards 🎉 🎉\n\nWe believe that OpenSea Mobile is a new type of onchain product that combines power & simplicity in a way not seen before\n\nWe’re also listening and learning — we believe that the world (us humans and agents) are inevitably coming onchain.\n\nWe believe that future will be mobile-first, it will be social, and mostly we believe it’ll be the next era of the cultural assets revolution that NFTs began.\n\nWe’re here for it. And we’re just getting started.\n\nTry it out, and let us know what you think 🙏👇\nhttp://opensea.io/r/chrismaddern", "name": "Chris Maddern", "handle": "chrismaddern", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1952689747849080832/bl89Lef3_200x200.jpg", "likes": 166, "rts": 10, "replies": 30, "views": 7115, "ts": 1792531917, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112654029595529229", "url": "https://x.com/opensea/status/2112654029595529229", "text": "OpenSea Mobile is now open to everyone.  \n\nEverything you own. Everything you trade. Everyone you trade with.  \n\nMemes, art, trading cards, perps. 25+ chains, all your wallets, one app.  \n\nTrade everything, together.", "name": "OpenSea", "handle": "opensea", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2112614202011537408/I-WGhmg2_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1767, "rts": 303, "replies": 545, "views": 199548, "ts": 1792530946, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112588539883843586/vid/avc1/1280x720/3s97S5mJ1pQINx-m.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112588539883843586/vid/avc1/1920x1080/nYtqw-Rkus3ooD7v.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112588539883843586/img/79r4M1L0NEPlqY8F.jpg", "dur": 84}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.94, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112546509250273370", "url": "https://x.com/thetripathi58/status/2112546509250273370", "text": "a lot of AI research eventually leads you back to the same handful of articles.\n\nQualitate is building its own source material: thousands of interviews with vetted experts each month, organized into research you can query. \n\n“Why did customers cut their spending?” often hasn’t been written down anywhere. Someone has to go ask. \n\nThe library is there before you arrive. You can find out what’s already known, then launch a custom study around the questions that are still open.", "name": "Chidanand Tripathi", "handle": "thetripathi58", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1887399788649586690/gJLTJ29F_200x200.jpg", "likes": 180, "rts": 39, "replies": 35, "views": 105916, "ts": 1792505311, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112544300751896702", "url": "https://x.com/S_Kadakia/status/2112544300751896702", "text": "We just raised $25M from Insight Partners to replace Gartner, McKinsey, and GLG.\n\nRIP the Quadrant, the 80-page consulting deck, and the $2000 expert network call.\n\nOur revenue run-rate is up 10x+ this year.\n\n100+ investment firms and enterprises use Qualitate to inform decisions with firsthand evidence.\n\nHere's how:\n\nhttps://www.qualitate.io/book-a-demo", "name": "Sagar Kadakia", "handle": "S_Kadakia", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2039423331938762752/vCFGOdIb_200x200.jpg", "likes": 733, "rts": 130, "replies": 137, "views": 296881, "ts": 1792504785, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112544190240358400/vid/avc1/1280x720/QaACj_QBWPQJcK__.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112544190240358400/vid/avc1/1920x1080/KgN176ObrVpGqv7K.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112544190240358400/img/Pw2JDRrY--NClwef.jpg", "dur": 133}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.94, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112263294031385028", "url": "https://x.com/tobi/status/2112263294031385028", "text": "This is extremely well crafted. You have to try it out", "name": "tobi lutke", "handle": "tobi", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1999293930936909824/_HWYanot_200x200.jpg", "likes": 738, "rts": 29, "replies": 25, "views": 89553, "ts": 1792437787, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112212804979880239", "url": "https://x.com/ekuyda/status/2112212804979880239", "text": "Wabi 2.0 is live!\n\npersonal agents are one person, one chat. but the parts of life that matter run on more than one person\n\nWabi is an agent you use together. you talk to it, it does stuff, builds the apps you need, and anyone can join the thread - your partner, your best friend, the preschool moms groupchat\n\nschool changes pickup time → Wabi updates the family calendar, everyone sees it.\na show you’d both love → Wabi finds a night that works, gets the tickets.\nthe trip everyone keeps talking about → Wabi picks the dates, builds the itinerary, books it\n\ngo start a thread with your people 👇", "name": "Eugenia Kuyda", "handle": "ekuyda", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2105081341352263680/H9RzWr7T_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1673, "rts": 218, "replies": 353, "views": 1848719, "ts": 1792425750, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112212457234284544/vid/avc1/1280x720/HW0ErfX-0u7kWbHU.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112212457234284544/vid/avc1/3840x2160/4gITKDb_F7iviaVH.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112212457234284544/img/Wzg-bjHfnRT2-0FG.jpg", "dur": 75}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.93, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112669039009104059", "url": "https://x.com/figma/status/2112669039009104059", "text": "Specs are here and they can do a lot\n\n→ Create data reports, PRDs, generate hand-off context\n→ Bring in outside context with an agent\n→ Turn rough ideas into a detailed spec\n→ Send it to a coding agent using Figma’s MCP server\n→ Build a Code Layer on top and refine", "name": "Figma", "handle": "figma", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2068849889753333760/YE3KJq___200x200.jpg", "likes": 161, "rts": 11, "replies": 24, "views": 13883, "ts": 1792534525, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112667483945496576/vid/avc1/1280x720/41GJoZLxCDq5wa7m.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112667483945496576/vid/avc1/1920x1080/rk5rY6mmLIfTM0VD.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112667483945496576/img/7cG8jFGOKBdhtL5G.jpg", "dur": 778}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.93, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112411101354942861", "url": "https://x.com/nazzari/status/2112411101354942861", "text": "Hired.", "name": "Bella", "handle": "nazzari", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037407835555057664/uIt9u40V_200x200.jpg", "likes": 511, "rts": 6, "replies": 7, "views": 83479, "ts": 1792473027, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112068761176121674", "url": "https://x.com/_darshi/status/2112068761176121674", "text": "Hi, it's Darshita. I am a designer.\n\nAnd I'm pitching myself in public 'cause I'm done with a year full of anxiety.\n\nEveryone says design is dead and AI killed it. But the real parasite was hiding in plain sight.\n\nSo here's my film, DESIGN IS DEAD. She's bold, fearless and very PINK 💖\n\nHiring? My DMs are open.", "name": "Darshita Patankar", "handle": "_darshi", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2112096367627976704/DxIoeke1_200x200.jpg", "likes": 41428, "rts": 2926, "replies": 1302, "views": 5081917, "ts": 1792391407, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112063508313767936/vid/avc1/1718x720/ElSippkBdAT5vgJF.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112063508313767936/vid/avc1/3840x1608/lgOlmN4hM0Yxo3se.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HU-ZIGybAAAOTRe.jpg", "dur": 250}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.93, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112610230043312618", "url": "https://x.com/testingcatalog/status/2112610230043312618", "text": "OpenAI ❤️ Orchestra Bio\n\n> OpenAI has acquired Orchestra Bio⁠ to work on Rosalind models and tools for life sciences research.\n\n> \"Orchestra Bio is a platform that helps biopharma teams coordinate the complex process of drug development.\"\n\nAI advancements in life sciences are probably one of the most desired areas for many. So far, it seems like a top priority for Anthropic, OpenAI, and Google.", "name": "🚨 AI News | TestingCatalog", "handle": "testingcatalog", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1899962463115751424/i-6MBWau_200x200.jpg", "likes": 217, "rts": 14, "replies": 12, "views": 10642, "ts": 1792520503, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVF_hgjXwAAb-j7.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2112607347688583586", "url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2112607347688583586", "text": "We’ve acquired Orchestra Bio, a platform that helps biopharma teams coordinate the complex process of drug development.\n\nTogether, we’ll build on Rosalind, our AI models and tools for life sciences research, to streamline those operations and help new treatments reach patients sooner.\n\nWelcome @ashokaraj_ and team!\n\nhttps://openai.com/index/openai-to-acquire-orchestra-bio/", "name": "OpenAI", "handle": "OpenAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1885410181409820672/ztsaR0JW_200x200.jpg", "likes": 5905, "rts": 522, "replies": 371, "views": 545241, "ts": 1792519816, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.92, "thread": [], "tier": "must"}, {"id": "2112567086904160455", "url": "https://x.com/daleverett/status/2112567086904160455", "text": "Today we’re launching WonderSearch (@ycombinator F26).\n\nIn 1977 we put everything humanity knew on one golden record and launched it into space.\n\nIn 2026 your AI agent still can’t find last week’s contract.\n\nWonderSearch is search for AI agents. It finds anything in your data, instantly, with zero embeddings: no vector database, just the exact passage and its source.\n\nThank you to all of our early users!\n\n@wondersearchai", "name": "dale", "handle": "daleverett", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2049549782755205121/y6qaHyA-_200x200.jpg", "likes": 142, "rts": 23, "replies": 57, "views": 8697, "ts": 1792510217, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564740748955648/vid/avc1/1280x720/fdwLhV7ZVkl1YMvp.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564740748955648/vid/avc1/1920x1080/1ZCDi5baWbQn1A2L.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112564740748955648/img/ZogCf485q7x_Ogyd.jpg", "dur": 37}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.92, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112645094540988549", "url": "https://x.com/AkoolInc/status/2112645094540988549", "text": "Your story deserves the big screen.\n\nBring your vision to life with AKOOL and submit your original film to the AKOOL AI Film Challenge. From the first frame to the final twist, show us what you can imagine.\n\nReady to roll? Visit Akool page for details.", "name": "Akool Inc", "handle": "AkoolInc", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1857138415109910528/iJ47_VAr_200x200.jpg", "likes": 202, "rts": 15, "replies": 3, "views": 11547, "ts": 1792528816, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112645041516691457/vid/avc1/1280x720/-7oQ88bIXsfBcOD8.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112645041516691457/vid/avc1/1920x1080/VDvDW8jr7Ony0FMo.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVGfhGnW4AALCa2.jpg", "dur": 38}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.92, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112664888409473269", "url": "https://x.com/dravenip/status/2112664888409473269", "text": "WHY ARE WE PAYING SO MUCH FOR BROWSER AGENTS?\n\nnace ai just launched drex for browser use, powered by drex max.\n\nthe numbers are kinda crazy:\n\n→ $2.80 per 1,000 miniwob++ tasks vs $31 with claude code\n\n→ frontier-level browser performance at a fraction of the cost\n\n→ $25 in free credits to get started\n\nif you're building agents that interact with the web, this is worth checking out.\n\nhttp://console.nace.ai", "name": "draven", "handle": "dravenip", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2094585676800860160/6Xm8L9f6_200x200.jpg", "likes": 188, "rts": 8, "replies": 13, "views": 12124, "ts": 1792533535, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112642726877405531", "url": "https://x.com/NaceAI/status/2112642726877405531", "text": "Drex for Browser Use is here!\nClaude Sonnet level accuracy at the fraction of the cost\n\n1,000 browser tasks:\nDrex Harness: $1.30\nClaude Code: $24\nCodex: $28\n\nStart here: https://console.nace.ai", "name": "Nace AI", "handle": "NaceAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1904211985488871426/z5Z5rKcl_200x200.jpg", "likes": 35, "rts": 3, "replies": 2, "views": 10948, "ts": 1792528251, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112641445072863232/vid/avc1/1280x720/23NgPCKVh98EcT2v.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112641445072863232/vid/avc1/1920x1080/z1L4KIGq6dUIF_hr.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112641445072863232/img/-LV0zfzJWhLJdvBA.jpg", "dur": 27}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.92, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112232332333900170", "url": "https://x.com/jang_yoel/status/2112232332333900170", "text": "Today, Dream Labs is out of stealth.\n\nIn February 2026, while we were at NVIDIA, @scott_e_reed @youliangtan @GeYunhao  and I started calling a new kind of robot model a World Action Model, one that learns how the world moves from video, then uses that to decide how to act.\n\nToday, we’re releasing Dream-1 through a public API that anyone in the world can use.\n\nWhen you rent a car you’ve never driven, you don’t learn to drive all over again. Within a few minutes, it feels like your own. Robots should work the same way: a good model should be able to pick up a new robot and get to work, without being retrained from scratch.\n\nThat’s what we’ve spent the last 6 months on, and it’s what Dream-1 does. It controls bimanual robots with parallel grippers it has never seen before, zero-shot, on unseen tasks in unseen environments.\n\nGeneralization has been my North Star in robotics: first by distilling video world models into VLAs (DreamGen), then by learning to act from those world models directly (DreamZero), and now by transferring across robots (Dream-1). I’ve come to believe it’s the only direction that lasts. Pushing a narrow model from 90% to 99.9% on a single task is real work, but much of it gets washed away once a model that generalizes arrives.\n\nSince the start of the company we’ve stayed single-minded about generalization.That focus is what got Dream-1 to control robots it was never trained on, on tasks it was never shown. And it’s what makes a public API possible at all: a model that only does one task on one robot can’t serve millions of users.\n\nDream-1 is still a research beta, and it will make mistakes. But it already drives cars it’s never seen.\n\nGeneralization wins in the end, and the end is closer than it looks.\n\nHere’s Dream-1 taking the wheel of a robot it’s never seen. Full details 👇", "name": "Joel Jang", "handle": "jang_yoel", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2110978621473189888/LKvpu6iN_200x200.jpg", "likes": 588, "rts": 59, "replies": 74, "views": 30863, "ts": 1792430406, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112232308795383809/vid/avc1/640x360/3TyEHWghhx4JI6uB.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112232308795383809/vid/avc1/1280x720/Dz17qP66Usa55Qgu.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112232308795383809/img/hoEpeTaGalSANxBg.jpg", "dur": 28}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.91, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}]);